From a5e77bc1f01dcdfac2721391f474e3eb3f3ecda8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: austin62jake <340374338+austin62jake@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:17:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cl): the text dump, is_prismatic and TiltedFrame keep the
 stated spindle C

cl::text wrote a C-live path without its C angle and is_prismatic read
it as a 3-axis path; TiltedFrame rebuilt moves with rotary: None
(#295). The dump now writes and reads the golden writer's SC word, a
path stating C is not prismatic (so the dump is v4), and world_path
copies the angle onto every move it maps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
